  p_Description_630c52d72b8b := 'Z.AI (Zhipu AI) high-speed serving variant of GLM-5.3-Flash, released 2026-09-18. Same capability base as GLM-5.3-Flash — native multimodal (text/image/video/agentic), 320B total / 18B active parameters on a hybrid sparse + linear attention MoE, 1M-token context and 131,072 max output — served at up to 200 tokens/s for roughly 2.5x the per-token price ($0.37/$1.25 against Flash''s $0.15/$0.50). FlashX is a serving and inference upgrade, not a separately documented intelligence checkpoint, so PowerRank matches GLM-5.3-Flash and only CostRank moves. Targeted at visual coding, tool use and long-horizon agent workloads that are latency-bound rather than quality-bound. Note that Z.AI added GLM-5.3-Flash to its GLM Coding Plan subscription but left FlashX off it, so FlashX is metered API only. Sources: https://openrouter.ai/z-ai/glm-5.3-flashx ; https://docs.z.ai/guides/vlm/glm-5.3-flash ; https://www.cometapi.com/what-is-glm-5-3-flashx/ ; https://www.orcarouter.ai/blog/glm-5-3-flashx-release ; https://apimaster.ai/blog/glm-5-3-flashx-api';
